Why: Linux background keys and pixel clicks work without /dev/uinput: the virtual pointer and keyboard pair is fed through its own XTEST devices (core events stay on: Xorg's software cursor keeps a no-core master's cursor without a reference, a use-after-free that aborts the server); keys reach the window under the pair's pointer (PointerRoot focus) so no window manager activates it; the focus guard stamps the user's window with a fresh user time so a dialog the app opens later can't take the front, restores an active window the window manager dropped, ignores a stacking list that was empty at capture, and the focus notes of real input stay on a line of their own.

